MixType Release History
=======================

MixType v0.4.0 — 2026-09-26
----------------------------------------

- Added versioned portable `.mixtypebackup` complete backup / restore.
- Backup includes portable preferences, active CIN/cassette, CHT/CHS Personal Lexicon,
  promotion/composition pending learning data, single-character preferences, user phrases,
  filters, replacements, associated phrases, and custom symbols.
- Restore relocates CIN and user data to the new Mac's local paths rather than preserving
  old absolute paths.
- Added validation, rollback, fail-closed malformed-package handling, and exact restore
  semantics for known portable roles.
- Added SwiftUI and Cocoa Backup / Restore UI with explicit replacement confirmation.
- Fixed Preferences being permanently forced above Save/Open panels and other apps.
- Fixed duplicate `.mixtypebackup.mixtypebackup` suggested filenames.
- Real-Mac export acceptance passed; release contains no private backup/CIN/learning data.

MixType v0.3.0 — 2026-09-26
----------------------------------------

- Completed Hybrid CIN + Pinyin routing and graduated mixed-token routing to default-on.
- Added Personal Lexicon, full-Pinyin / initials / mixed-prefix lookup and adaptive learning.
- Added single-character preference learning and composition phrase learning.
- Added continuous Chinese-Pinyin / English mixed candidates such as
  `jintianmeetinggai → 今天meeting改`.
- Added protected ASCII handling for model names, identifiers, e-mail, URLs and
  digit-leading units/time such as `server2026`, `MacBookM6`, `3pm`, `20kW`, and `300RT`.
- Preserved valid CIN punctuation-code precedence such as `s. → ？`.

